WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.003 line:92%
How's everybody doing tonight?

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.105 line:92%
That is so wonderful to hear

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:05.805 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Let's get to the news.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
Today is the 100th day
of Joe Biden's presidency.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:11.011 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Wow, that's crazy.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.280 line:92%
It's felt like exactly 100 days.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.417
President Biden was greeted with
standing applause last night

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:18.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he entered
the House Chamber

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
to deliver his first
joint address to Congress.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:22.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ All groaning ]

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.594 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Ooooouuuuuch!

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.030 line:92%
-Way, way too many groans.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:30.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:32.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys, when we used to
have an audience,

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
we would test material
earlier in the day.

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.669 line:92%
And so, now, a lot of times,

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm seeing things
for the first time, as you do.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:42.909 line:92%
And sometimes, we get it wrong

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughing ]

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
During his first
address last night

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:48.748 line:92%
to a joint session of Congress

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:51.117
President Biden called on
Democrats and Republicans

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.220
to come together to pass
police reform legislation,

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.891 size:81% position:41%
though not everybody
stood up for that one.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
President Biden
called on Congress last nigh

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:02.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
to create a new agency to
develop breakthrough treatment

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:07.367
for diseases such as Alzheimer's
and cancer -- and who knows?

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.736 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Maybe even narcolepsy.

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:11.938 line:92%
The 2021 NFL Draft began today

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the Jacksonville Jaguars
have the first pick.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:18.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
Said a spokesman,
"Great, we pick Orlando."

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:21.881
In a new interview, a doctor and
clinical consultant for NASA

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
said that sex in space
would be difficult.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.685 line:92%
When asked why, the doctor said,

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, we've been married
a long time."

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:33.793
According to new research,
gossiping about other people

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.328 line:92%
can have positive effects.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:37.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, you know
who should try it, then?

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.833 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Whispers ] Ashley.

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:40.900 line:92%
Microsoft announced yesterda

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:44.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it will retire
its default font, "Calibri,"

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.006
and replace it with one of these
five new typefaces --

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:51.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tenorite, Bierstadt, Skeena,
Seaford, and Grandview.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:55.515
Either that, or Microsoft is
opening a day-care in Brooklyn

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Skeena!

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:59.619 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Grandview, Tenorite!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.957 line:92%
Stop -- Stop teasing Grandview

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.993 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's a Bierstadt!

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:10.163 line:92%
Of the Long Island Bierstadts.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:12.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
A greep --
A group, excuse me.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:16.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm bummed that I messed u
the top of this joke.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:18.138 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't hold it
against the writer

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.342 line:92%
that I flubbed at the top.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.343 line:92%
'Cause every now and then,

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's one that's
so pristine...

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.649 line:92%
Bays already said this was -

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.085
and I hope you don't mind me
putting words in your mouth --

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.621 line:92%
the best joke he's ever written.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
A group of elite
classical cellists in Denmar

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
recently performed
an outdoor concert

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.427 size:75% position:38% line:92%
for a group of cows.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.396 line:92%
Said the cows, "They were good

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.765 line:92%
but they're no Yo-Yo Moo."

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.739 line:92%
We have to legally tell yo

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:56.042 line:92%
that if you've heard that joke

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.410 line:92%
even if you're double-vaxxed

00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:59.412 line:92%
you can catch coronavirus.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.347 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.583 line:92%
[ Laughs ] It makes no sense

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:04.117 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Yo-Yo Moo."

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:09.122
It only makes sense if the onl
noise Yo-Yo Ma made was "Ma.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:14.861 line:92%
This is the other thing --

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
not to tell you
how things used to be

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:18.431 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and how things are now.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.300 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Writers used to come in,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'd read
all the jokes together.

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:26.973
And so, as I read it, they would
have to look me in the face.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:28.441 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And now, they don't.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.611 size:81% position:41%
They just sit at home
and send in Yo-Yo Moo.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.015
According to new research, the
night shift mode on your phone

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:37.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
does not help you
sleep better at night,

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:41.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
because at the end of the day,
you know what you did.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally, a rare
bottle of bourbon

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is believed to have bee
produced before 1802

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:47.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
will go up for auction
later this year

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is expected to sell
for up to $40,000.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
Meanwhile, an NFT
of a photo of it

00:03:52.332 --> 00:03:55.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
is expected to sell
for $7 billion.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:57.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that was
the monologue, everybody!

